Program:
#include <stdio.h>
long long factorial(int n)
{
    if (n == 0 || n == 1)
        return 1;
    return n * factorial(n - 1);
}
int main()
{
    int n;
    scanf("%d", &n);
    printf("%lld\n", factorial(n));
    return 0;
}
Sample Input:
6
Output:
720
Explanation:
The base case is factorial(0) = 1. For n > 0, the function calls itself with n-1 until it reaches 0.
